# Copy to .env (never committed): `make` reads it. Or export the variables in your shell.
# Where the lake lives: a local folder (default .lake) or a GCS bucket.
CITYPULSE_LAKE_URI=.lake
# CITYPULSE_LAKE_URI=gs://citypulse-tr-dev-lake
# Where `citypulse load` writes (make sets it from ENV): the BigQuery project.
# CITYPULSE_BQ_PROJECT=citypulse-tr-dev
# make shortcuts: ENV=dev|prod picks the project; LAKE=gcs points ingest at that project's bucket.
